<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 13 February, from 962 to 2008.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/962">962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,064 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Otto I issues the Diploma Ottonianum to Pope John XII</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The newly crowned emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a> issued a charter to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xii">Pope John XII</a> confirming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>'s possession of the lands granted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a>. It also required each newly elected pope to swear loyalty before imperial envoys prior to consecration.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diploma-ottonianum">Diploma Ottonianum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xii">Pope John XII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1258">1258 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">768 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols begin the sack of Baghdad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a>'s troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and began a week of killing and plunder. Libraries and the city's great institutions of learning were destroyed, and tens of thousands of inhabitants died.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1462">1462 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">564 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward IV signs a secret treaty with the Lord of the Isles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iv-of-england">Edward IV of England</a> agreed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-islay">John of Islay, Lord of the Isles</a>, and the exiled Earl of Douglas that a conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> would be divided between John and Douglas as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Its discovery cost John the earldom of Ross.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-westminster-ardtornish">Treaty of Westminster-Ardtornish</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iv-of-england">Edward IV of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-of-the-isles">Lord of the Isles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1542">1542 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">484 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catherine Howard is executed at the Tower of London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s fifth wife, still a teenager, was beheaded for adultery and treason. She was the second of his queens to be executed, after her cousin Anne Boleyn.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1633">1633 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">393 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo arrives in Rome to face the Inquisition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Summoned over his 'Dialogue Concerning the Two Chief World Systems', <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Tried that spring, he was forced to abjure the view that the Earth moves and spent his last years under house arrest.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1689">1689 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">337 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William III and Mary II offered the English crown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Banqueting House, the Convention Parliament presented the Declaration of Rights and offered the throne jointly to William and Mary. The settlement limited royal power and confirmed Parliament's role.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1861">1861 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fortress of Gaeta surrenders, ending the Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a three-month siege by Piedmontese forces, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaeta">Gaeta</a> and went into exile. Weeks later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> was proclaimed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-ii">Victor Emmanuel II</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied bombers begin the destruction of Dresden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and then American raids over two days created a firestorm that killed about 25,000 people and destroyed the historic centre. The attack's justification has been debated ever since.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2008">2008 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">18 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kevin Rudd apologises to the Stolen Generations</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s Prime Minister delivered a formal apology in Parliament to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people taken from their families under past government policies.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 February <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mary-of-burgundy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mary-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mary of Burgundy</span><span class="tp">1457–1482</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elijah-levita"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Elijah Levita</span><span class="tp">1469–1549</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georgios-papandreou"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georgios-papandreou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georgios Papandreou</span><span class="tp">1888–1968</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aung-san"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aung-san.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aung San</span><span class="tp">1915–1947</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/omar-torrijos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/omar-torrijos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Omar Torrijos</span><span class="tp">1929–1981</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 13 February <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stefan-nemanja"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stefan-nemanja.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stefan Nemanja</span><span class="tp">c. 1113–1199</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andronikos-ii-palaiologos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andronikos-ii-palaiologos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andronikos II Palaiologos</span><span class="tp">1259–1332</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-stuart-queen-of-bohemia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elizabeth-stuart-queen-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Elizabeth Stuart, Queen of Bohemia</span><span class="tp">1596–1662</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ruder-boskovic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ruder-boskovic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ruđer Bošković</span><span class="tp">1711–1787</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
